Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: reject backwards MT7981 survey snapshots

MT7981 firmware can return an older channel MIB snapshot even when the
reply has the expected offsets. Subtracting the previous unsigned
counters then wraps survey totals. Clamping individual deltas while
rebasing onto the older sample also counts the same interval again when
the newer snapshot returns.

Reject the whole backwards MT7981 sample without changing totals or the
baseline. Keep the existing reply validation and bounded retries. An
explicit channel switch or counter reset still establishes a new baseline
through chan_switch, including when the new counters are lower.

This prevents unsigned underflow and duplicate accumulation on a return
to an earlier snapshot. It cannot identify an incorrect but increasing
per-band snapshot returned by firmware.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/issues/1135

--- a/mt7915/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7915/mcu.c
@@ -3343,6 +3343,17 @@
 	if (chan_switch)
 		goto out;
 
+	/* Do not rebase onto an older MT7981 firmware snapshot. */
+	if (is_mt7981(&dev->mt76) &&
+	    (cc_tx < state_ts->cc_tx ||
+	     __res_u64(2) < state_ts->cc_bss_rx ||
+	     __res_u64(2) + __res_u64(3) < state_ts->cc_rx ||
+	     __res_u64(0) + cc_tx + __res_u64(2) + __res_u64(3) <
+						state_ts->cc_busy)) {
+		dev_kfree_skb(skb);
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	state->cc_tx += cc_tx - state_ts->cc_tx;
 	state->cc_bss_rx += __res_u64(2) - state_ts->cc_bss_rx;
 	state->cc_rx += __res_u64(2) + __res_u64(3) - state_ts->cc_rx;
